    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2BwDJuqNETEyCwswgX8zTyT)_\n\n## What\n\n- New `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-add-all-tables` (`C-u` is a dry run): every litnote tagged `book`, `collection`, `reference` or `encyclopedia` gets its `collection-query-table` block, also when no chapter note exists yet, so the table is there when the first chapter note is made.\n  - The tags are `sp-litnotes-meta-parent-tags`; the view follows the tag (`book-sections`, `collection-articles`, `reference-entries`, `encyclopedia-articles`).\n  - Only notes that also carry the `litnote` tag are touched; other notes tagged `book` are left alone.\n  - A note that already has a block keeps it and the block is refreshed. Same summary buffer and database sync as `sp-litnotes-meta-refresh-all-tables` (#386), which it extends (new `ALL-PARENTS` argument).\n- Doc updated in `sp-litnotes-meta.org`; `.el` re-tangled.\n\n## Tests\n\n- New ERT test with stubbed Vulpea (dry run, insert per tag, non-litnote untouched, second run adds nothing); all 62 litnotes-meta tests pass on Emacs 29.3; `tools/check-tangle.sh` passes.\n- Not run on the real vault. Run `C-u M-x sp-litnotes-meta-add-all-tables` first to see the list.\n- CHANGELOG not edited.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDSHDEGNJxmSPXp8cZ)_",
